<title>EGYPT: Egypt food firm paying 4.37 pounds.</title>
<headline>Egypt food firm paying 4.37 pounds.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-01-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Egyptian company Nasr Dehydrated and Agricultural Products said on Sunday it was paying an annual dividend of 4.37 pounds a share for 1995/6.</p>
<p>In September the state sold the private sector 59.4 percent of the 800,000 shares in the company.</p>
<p>The company made net after-tax profits of 5.12 million pounds ($1.51 million) in 1995/6, which ended on June 30, up from 4.61 million in 1994/5.</p>
<p>The dividend is payable from January 9 from branches of the Bank of Alexandria.</p>
<p>$1 = 3.40 pounds</p>
<p>-- Cairo newsroom +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
</text>
